+// expect-error: NITPICK-RESOLVE-010
+//
+// PROBE 13 -- AN ERRNO NAMED BY THE PROGRAM, WITH ITS CODE.
+//
+// ASKS: may a library name a kernel errno the prelude does not -- `error:EInProgress = 115i32;`, so
+// that `connect`'s answer could be compared with it? The prelude names five beside `IoEof`
+// (`WouldBlock`, `Interrupted`, `NotFound`, `Exists`, `CrossDevice`) and says naming more "is a
+// decision for the code that needs it".
+// DEPENDS ON THE ANSWER: SK-014 (`connect`'s `EINPROGRESS`), SK-031 (the accept loop's error
+// table) and `SAFETY.md` S-6: what this library can tell apart, and what it can only forward.
+// EXPECTED: refused, `NITPICK-RESOLVE-010` at the declaration -- an explicit error code is the
+// prelude's alone (D-179) -- and nothing else. Probe 13b asks the other way in: a cast.
+mod:probe13_errno_declared;
+
+error:EInProgress = 115i32;
+
+func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) {
+    exit 0i32;
+};
